# pipeline/export.py now writes the monthly flow export pre-split by year
# (dashboard_flow_monthly_YYYY.json, ~35-45MB each — those ARE tracked
# normally). This just guards against ever committing the old single-file
# form, which exceeds GitHub's 100MB per-file push limit.
public/data/dashboard_flow_monthly.json

# Same reasoning, for dashboard_flow_quarterly.json — now split one file
# per dimension (dashboard_flow_quarterly_<dimension>.json) so the frontend
# only fetches the dimension a reader actually has selected. The old single
# ~110MB blob is never committed again.
public/data/dashboard_flow_quarterly.json
